60,3,1,talk,May,,"I'll go with the Meeting Space. It solves the ""first come, first served"" chaos with a calendar.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I prefer the Quiet Room. It's the only way to ensure the office stays peaceful and clean.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,The Meeting Space addresses the waste of funds and the lack of a proper venue for discussion.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Meeting Space for sure! No more outside invoices!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Meeting Space. It's the best way to bring us together and handle the tough talks.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, wouldn't a calendar for a meeting space also keep the noise organized?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Perhaps, but it doesn't solve the thin wall problem.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"We can manage the noise with rules, but we cannot easily manage the loss of money.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Yay! It looks like we're mostly agreeing!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,It's the most versatile choice.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
